    <scope doc="Module/script to &quot;compile&quot; all .py files to .pyc (or .pyo) file. When called as a script with arguments, this compiles the directories given as arguments recursively; the -l option prevents it from recursing into directories.  Without arguments, if compiles all modules on sys.path, without recursing into subdirectories.  (Even though it should do so for packages -- for now, you&apos;ll have to deal with packages separately.)  See module py_compile for details of the actual byte-compilation." ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="compileall">
