    <scope doc="Routines to help recognizing sound files. Function whathdr() recognizes various types of sound file headers. It understands almost all headers that SOX can decode.  The return tuple contains the following items, in this order: - file type (as SOX understands it) - sampling rate (0 if unknown or hard to decode) - number of channels (0 if unknown or hard to decode) - number of frames in the file (-1 if unknown or hard to decode) - number of bits/sample, or &apos;U&apos; for U-LAW, or &apos;A&apos; for A-LAW " ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="sndhdr">
