    <scope doc="Base64 content transfer encoding per RFCs 2045-2047. This module handles the content transfer encoding method defined in RFC 2045 to encode arbitrary 8-bit data using the three 8-bit bytes in four 7-bit characters encoding known as Base64.  It is used in the MIME standards for email to attach images, audio, and text using some 8-bit character sets to messages.  This module provides an interface to encode and decode both headers and bodies with Base64 encoding. " ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="email.base64mime">
