    <scope doc="Word completion for GNU readline 2.0. This requires the latest extension to the readline module. The completer completes keywords, built-ins and globals in a selectable namespace (which defaults to __main__); when completing NAME.NAME..., it evaluates (!) the expression up to the last dot and completes its attributes.  It&apos;s very cool to do &quot;import sys&quot; type &quot;sys.&quot;, hit the completion key (twice), and see the list of names defined by the sys module!  Tip: to use the tab key as the completion key, call" ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="rlcompleter">
      <scope classrefs="object" doc=" " ilk="class" line="41" lineend="150" name="Completer">
