    <scope doc="Fixer for __metaclass__ = X -&gt; (metaclass=X) methods. The various forms of classef (inherits nothing, inherits once, inherints many) don&apos;t parse the same in the CST so we look at ALL classes for a __metaclass__ and if we find one normalize the inherits to all be an arglist.  For one-liner classes (&apos;class X: pass&apos;) there is no indent/dedent so we normalize those into having a suite.  Moving the __metaclass__ into the classdef can also cause the class body to be empty so there is some special casing for that as well." ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="lib2to3.fixes.fix_metaclass">
