        <scope doc="If E has a .keys() method, does:     for k in E: D[k] = E[k] If E lacks .keys() method, does:     for (k, v) in E: D[k] = v In either case, this is followed by: for k in F: D[k] = F[k]" ilk="function" name="update" signature="D.update(E, **F) -&gt; None.  Update D from dict/iterable E and F." />
