      <scope classrefs="object" doc="kevent(ident, filter=KQ_FILTER_READ, flags=KQ_EV_ADD, fflags=0, data=0, udata=0) This object is the equivalent of the struct kevent for the C API.  See the kqueue manpage for more detailed information about the meaning of the arguments.  One minor note: while you might hope that udata could store a reference to a python object, it cannot, because it is impossible to keep a proper reference count of the object once it&apos;s passed into the kernel. Therefore, I have restricted it to only storing an integer.  I recommend ignoring it and simply using the &apos;ident&apos; field to key off" ilk="class" name="kevent">
